{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401053-help-me-understand-white-reaper","id":1401053,"title":"Help Me Understand White Reaper","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-04T22:10:50-07:00","id":1401053,"title":"Help Me Understand White Reaper","content":"I only recently realized that I've been using White Reaper wrong for over two years now, so I want to make sure I have it right.<br /> <br /> You generate a halo when you are in the form charm and you crash a non-trivial enemy or damage a battle group.<br /> <br /> Whenever you use Bleeding Crescent Strike, Greatest Killer Attitude, Enemies Like Grass, or Snow Follows Winter, <u>you lose all your halos at the end of your turn</u>.<br /> <br /> The upside of the underlined bit is that you can stack as many of those charms as you like and they all benefit from your collected halos.<br /> <br /> The downside of the underlined bit is that if you gain halos with an attack that uses any of those charms, you still lose them at the end of your turn.<br /> <br /> Do I have that right? Do you really only have one WR charm you can use to actually generate Halos that don't go away at the end of your turn? How on earth are you expected to ever have more that two of the things, if it means locking yourself out of your best charms? Am I misreading this? Or is it just the expectation that you'll only ever really have one or so, unless you're fighting a battle group and just used Enemies Like Grass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24146-pfm1995","name":"pfm1995","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24146_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T02:12:34-07:00","id":1401079,"title":"","content":"White Reaper wants to fight multiple opponents, this is because it has the ability to crash more people and potentially get more halos. Even the default charms without halo use are fairly strong.<br /> <br /> I've made White Reaper expansion charms, and I've done some things to help address the way to get additional halos (EX: First time in a scene you'd gain 1, you automatically gain an additional one) but in the end you'd still like to be outnumbered.<br /> <br /> It is a drawback to the style, but I don't think a strong one. Being one of the only styles in the game that's good on taking on multiple opponents at once is pretty nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T09:35:26-07:00","id":1401136,"title":"","content":"Actually, you don't lose those halos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page956\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page956\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page956\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page956 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T10:28:22-07:00","id":1401145,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I really hate Core. Thanks for the link!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24146-pfm1995","name":"pfm1995","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24146_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T11:24:39-07:00","id":1401154,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure the intent of white reaper is that you don't often get more than 2 halos unless you're fighting a battlegroup. It takes until Essence 3 before you can even have more than two anyway, and even then only by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}